{
	title: 'Design demo pages under /demo',
	spec: 'The web endpoint serves design demo pages: GET /demo/<name>, where name is lowercase letters, digits and dashes, answers src/web/demo/<name>.html with the theme CSS (web.css()) in place of /*COLORS*/, no-store, and a content security policy that allows only inline style and script. Any other name, or a file that does not exist, is 404; the path never reaches the file system unchecked. Demo pages need a login like every page: without the cookie the gate is shown, and ?auth=<code> redeems like on other pages. A demo page is a standalone HTML file for comparing UI alternatives side by side with the real theme colors; like the rest of src/web it holds no color literals. src/web/demo/ui-review.html (artifact ui-review.html) puts the ui-craft review findings (selection color, composer vertical centering, tab label alignment, question layout, focus style, notice bar width, spacing scale, fold motion, small text) as options side by side; the chosen option and an optional note per item, and general notes, are kept in localStorage and turned into plain text in a read-only box with a Copy button, to paste into a Hal prompt.',
	status: 'done',
	needs: ['8a']
}
